PART 1 — hidden orders (synthetic SYN-ALPHA, tick 0.50, lot 0.001; local prototype, no funds)

▸ syn-maker-a: displayed ask 0.500 @ 2001.00
    private[syn-maker-a] accepted sell 0.500 @ 2001.00 (displayed)
    public #3 level sell 2001.00 = 0.500
▸ syn-maker-a: displayed bid 0.500 @ 1999.00
    private[syn-maker-a] accepted buy 0.500 @ 1999.00 (displayed)
    public #4 level buy 1999.00 = 0.500
▸ syn-maker-b: HIDDEN ask 2.000 @ 2000.50 (inside the spread)
    private[syn-maker-b] accepted sell 2.000 @ 2000.50 (hidden)
    public: (nothing published)
    public book: bids [0.500@1999.00] asks [0.500@2001.00]
    → the hidden order produced no public message and no public sequence gap.

▸ syn-taker-c: IOC buy 1.000 @ 2001.00
    private[syn-taker-c] accepted buy 1.000 @ 2001.00 (displayed)
    private[syn-taker-c] fill taker buy 1.000 @ 2000.50 → filled, leaves 0.000
    public #5 trade 1.000 @ 2000.50 (aggressor buy)
    → price priority: the better-priced hidden ask fills first; the print shows price and size only.

▸ syn-maker-a: displayed ask 0.300 @ 2000.50 (same price as the hidden remainder, later in time)
    private[syn-maker-a] accepted sell 0.300 @ 2000.50 (displayed)
    public #6 level sell 2000.50 = 0.300
▸ syn-taker-c: IOC buy 0.500 @ 2000.50
    private[syn-taker-c] accepted buy 0.500 @ 2000.50 (displayed)
    private[syn-taker-c] fill taker buy 0.300 @ 2000.50 → partially-filled, leaves 0.200
    private[syn-taker-c] fill taker buy 0.200 @ 2000.50 → filled, leaves 0.000
    public #7 trade 0.500 @ 2000.50 (aggressor buy)
    public #8 level sell 2000.50 = 0.000
    → displayed priority: at one price the displayed order fills before the earlier hidden one;
      the two maker fills are published as one aggregated print.
    → residual inference: the print (0.500) exceeds the displayed quantity removed (0.300), so an
      observer can infer that ≥ 0.200 traded against non-displayed liquidity at 2000.50.

▸ syn-maker-b: IOC buy against its own hidden ask (STP cancel-taker)
    private[syn-maker-b] accepted buy 0.100 @ 2000.50 (displayed)
    private[syn-maker-b] cancelled b2: self-trade-prevention (filled 0.000)
    public: (nothing published)
▸ syn-taker-c: post-only bid 0.100 @ 2000.00 (does not cross)
    private[syn-taker-c] accepted buy 0.100 @ 2000.00 (displayed, post-only)
    public #9 level buy 2000.00 = 0.100
▸ syn-taker-c: post-only bid @ 2000.50 (would take hidden liquidity)
    private[syn-taker-c] rejected c4: post-only-would-take
    public: (nothing published)
    → known leakage channel: a post-only rejection inside the spread reveals hidden liquidity;
      such rejections are throttled per account (docs/venue/MATCHING-RULES.md, rule H-7).

▸ syn-taker-c: tries to cancel maker-b's order by its client id
    private[syn-taker-c] cancel refused: unknown-order
    public: (nothing published)
    → another account's order is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.

